hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1981","Anba Abdah bin Abdullah, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Aws, on the authority of Umm Abdullah, the wife of Abu Musa, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of us shave. And he stung, and he broke.”"
"1982","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sahm bin Munjab, on the authority of Al-Qarth’, he said: When Abu Moses, his wife shouted, and he said: Did you not know what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? She said: Yes, then she remained silent, and it was said to her after that: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cursed the one who shaved, cut, or pierced someone.”"
"1983","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Usama bin Zaid told me, he said: You sent A daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to him, that a son of mine had been arrested, so he came to us, and he sent to read the greeting and say: “Indeed, what God has taken, And he has what He has given, and each has an appointed term, so let her be patient and seek reward.” So she sent a message to him swearing that he would come to her, so he stood up. And with him were Saad bin Ubadah, Muadh bin Jabal, Ubayy bin Ka’b, Zayd bin Thabit and some men, so he was taken to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted the boy while his soul was rattling, and his eyes filled with tears. Saad said: O Messenger of God, what is this? He said: “This is a mercy that God places in the hearts of His servants, and God only shows mercy to those of His merciful servants.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abu Uthman is Al-Nahdi, his name is Abdul Rahman bin Mull (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1984","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: I heard Anas, saying: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Patience at the first shock.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1985","Abba Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Iyas told us, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet and prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, and there was a son of his with him. He said: “Do you love him?” He said: May God love you as I love him. Then he died, and he lost him. They asked about him, and they said: He died, O Messenger of God! He said: “What makes you happy is that you do not approach one of the gates of Paradise unless you find it then striving to open it for you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abu Iyas's name is Muawiyah bin Qurrah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1986","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, who said: Abba Abdullah, who said: Abba Amr bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, that Amr bin Shuaib wrote to Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hussein consoled him over a son of his who had died. He mentioned in his book that he heard his father, Shuaib bin Muhammad, speaking on the authority of his grandfather. Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Asi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is not satisfied with His faithful servant if he goes With the purest of the people of the earth, he was patient and sought reward and said: “God has not commanded him to receive a reward less than Paradise.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Amr Bin Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, and they are three brothers: Amr, Omar, and Shuaib bin and Shuaib. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1987","Abba Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh said: Abba Ibn Wahb reported, Amr said: Bukayr bin Abdullah narrated to me, on the authority of Imran bin Nafi’, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever counts three of his loins will enter Paradise.” Then a woman stood up and said: Or two? He said: “Or two.” The woman said: I wish I had said one. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Bukayr: He is the son of Abdullah bin al-Ashjaj, and they are Three brothers: Yaqoub, Bukair, and Omar, and the oldest of them, and the one who speaks the most, is Bukair."
"1988","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Jarir, he said: Talq bin Muawiyah narrated to me, and Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to me, he said: My grandfather Talq bin Muawiyah narrated to me, On the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a son of hers who was complaining, and she said: Oh Messenger of God, I fear for him, and I presented three, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have been kept under intense protection by \fire\"""""""
"1989","Abba Yusuf bin Hammad Al-Basri, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz, meaning Ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no Muslim who has three people who have not yet reached the age of breaking oaths, but God admits him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them.”"
"1990","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sa’sa’a bin Muawiyah, he said: I met Abu Dhar, I said: Tell me, he said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are no two Muslims among whom three children who have not yet reached the age of perjury, except that God will forgive them, by His mercy toward them.”"
"1991","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “None of the Muslims should have three children die, and the Fire will touch them, unless the oath is fulfilled.”"
"1992","Anba Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya, and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam, said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no two Muslims among whom three children who have not reached the age of “Until our parents enter,” he said, “and they say, ‘Enter Paradise. Then it will be said to them: Enter Paradise, you and your parents. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1993","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim said: Abba Suleiman bin Harb said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Anas: “Anba The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned Zaid and Ja’far before news of them came. He mourned them while his eyes shed tears."
"1994","Anba Abu Dawud said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah and Ibn al-Musayyab told me that Abu Hurairah told them: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned for them the Negus, the companion of Abyssinia, the day he died, and said:” “Ask forgiveness for your brother.”"
"1995","Ubayd Allah ibn Fadhalah ibn Ibrahim informed me, saying: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri reported, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid informed me. Al-Muqri, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Rabia bin Saif Al-Maafiri told me, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: While we were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he saw a woman whom we do not think he knew. When the road reached the middle of the road, he stopped until it ended, and he saw Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said to her: “What brought you out of Your house, O Fatima? She said: I came to the people of this house, and I had compassion for them and consoled them for their death. He said: Perhaps you conveyed the message of God with them. Al-Kudda.” She said: “God forbid that I should have conveyed it when I heard you mentioning about that what you mention.” He said: “If I had conveyed it with them, I would not have seen it.” “Paradise until your father’s grandfather sees it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1996","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Umm Atiya al-Ansariyya said: A messenger entered upon us. When his daughter died, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wash her three or five or more than that, if you see that, with water.” And Sidr, and in the Hereafter make camphor or something of camphor. So when you have finished, then inform me.” And when we had finished, we informed him, and he gave us his loins. And he said: “Show it to her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1997","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, the servant of Umm Qais bint Muhsin, on the authority of Umm Qays said: My son died, so I mourned for him, so I said to the one who was washing him, “Do not wash my son with cold water.” So Okasha bin Muhsin went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he informed him of what she had said. He smiled, then said: “What she said is her life will be long,” so we do not know. A woman who lived as long as she lived"
"1998","Abba Yusuf bin Saeed said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ayoub said: And I heard Hafsa say: Umm Atiya told us that they They made the head of the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, three horns. I said: We broke it and made it three horns? ! She said: “Yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1999","Anba Amr bin Mansour said: Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Attiyah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about washing his daughter: “Start with her right side and the places where ablution is performed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2000","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, he said: Hafsa told us, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, she said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so he sent for us and said: “Wash her with water and lotus leaves, and wash her once, three or Five or seven, if you see that, and put in the afterlife some camphor, and when you have finished, then inform me. So when we finished, we announced him. So he presented to us his loins and said: “Give it to her.” She said: “And We combed it through three horns and left it behind it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2001","Abba Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Yazid, said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: The Messenger of God entered upon us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him when his daughter died, and he said: “Wash her three or five or more than that, if you see, with water and lotus leaves. And in the Hereafter, make camphor or something of camphor, and when you have finished, then inform me.” So when we had finished, we informed him, and he rolled up his loins to us and said: Make her feel it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2002","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Atiya, who said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. peace be upon him, and he said: “Wash it three, or five, or seven, or more than that, if you see that, with water and lotus leaves, and make In the Hereafter, camphor or something of camphor. When you have finished, let me know. So when we have finished, we announce to him, so he threw up his loins to us and said: Make her feel it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2003","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiya, and something similar, that he said: “Three, or Five, or seven, or more than that, if you see me.”"
"2004","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Bishr told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Alqama, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of some of his brothers, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, She said: The daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so he ordered us to wash her, and he said: “Wash her three, or five, or seven. Or more than that, if you see it.” She said: I said: Odd. He said: “Yes, and in the Hereafter make camphor or something of camphor, then “I had finished, so he informed me.” When we had finished, we informed him, so he gave us his rights and said, “Give her to her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2005","Anba Amr bin Zurarah Al-Naysaburi said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. May God bless him and grant him peace while we were washing his daughter. He said: “Wash her three or five or more than that, if you see that, with water and lotus leaves.” And in the Hereafter put camphor or something of camphor, and when you have finished, then inform me.” And when we had finished, we informed him, and he threw up his loins to us, and said: “Give it a hair.” He said: Hafsa said: We combed it three times, or five times, or seven times. He said: Umm Atiyah said: We combed it three times. Horns. Anba Qutaybah said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, and Hafsa said: On the authority of Umm Atiya: We made her head three horns. Anba Muhammad b. Mansour, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Hafsa told me, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: And We made her head Three centuries (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2006","Anba Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ayoub bin Abi Tamimah told me that he heard Muhammad bin Sirin says: Umm Atiyya was an Ansar woman. She came to avoid a son of hers, but she did not catch him. She told us, saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. peace be upon him while we were washing his daughter, and he said: “Wash her three, or five, or seven, or more than that, if you see, with water.” And Sidr, and in the Hereafter use camphor or something of camphor. When you have finished, then inform me. So when we finished, he threw out his loins to us and said: Show her to him.” And he did not say more than that. He said: I do not know which of his daughters? I said: What is the saying: Make her feel, shall I be tied? He said: I don't see it as anything other than him saying: He ruined it in it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2007","Anba Shuaib bin Yusuf, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Aoun reported, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: One of the daughters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Wash it three or five times or more than that, if you think so, and wash it with Sidr and water, and make At the end of that, camphor or something of camphor, so when you have finished, call me to it. She said: When we finished, we announced to him, and he threw up his loins to us, and said: “Make her feel this way.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2008","Abba Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Raqqi and Yusuf bin Sa`id al-Masisi, and the wording is his, said: Hajjaj, who is the son of Muhammad al-A'war, told us on the authority of Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech, and he mentioned a man from His companions died, so he was buried at night, and was shrouded in a useless shroud, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, discouraged the burial of a person at night unless it was necessary. In addition, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you takes care of his brother, let him shroud himself well.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2009","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Abi Orouba speaking, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Put on your white clothes, for they are purer and better, and shroud “Therein are your dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2010","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet was shrouded May God bless him and grant him peace, in three white garments.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2011","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ He was shrouded in three white robes, without a shirt or turban.”"
"2012","Abba Qutaibah said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in three White Yemeni robes like a cloak, with neither a shirt nor a turban.” He said: Then it was mentioned to Aisha their saying: “In two garments and a garment of ink,” she said. He was brought in hail, but they turned him back and did not shroud him in it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2013","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: “ When Abdullah bin Ubayy died, his son came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Give me your shirt so that I can shroud him in it, and pray for him. And he asked forgiveness for him, so he gave him his shirt. Then he said: “If you have finished, then allow me to pray for him.” Then Omar pulled him away and said: “God has forbidden you.” To pray for the hypocrites.” He said: I am between two choices. He said: “Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them.” So he prayed for him, and God revealed:"
"2014","Anba Abd al-Jabbar bin al-Ala bin Abd al-Jabbar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, heard Jabir saying: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came The grave of Abdullah bin Ubayy was placed in its pit. He stood over it, ordered him to be taken out, placed him on his knees, and clothed him. his shirt, and blew some of his saliva on it, for God knows best.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2015","Abba Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman is Al-Zuhri Al-Basri, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: “It was Al-Abbas was in Medina, so the Ansar asked for a garment to cover him, but they did not find a suitable shirt for him except the shirt of Abdullah bin Ubayy, so they covered him with it. \Eh\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2016","Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Anba Ismail bin Masoud told us: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, he said: I heard Al-Amash, he said: I heard a brother, he said: Khabbab told us, he said: “We emigrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking the face of God.” God Almighty, so our reward is obligatory for God. Among us is he who died without eating anything of his reward. Among them was Mus’ab bin Umair. He was killed on the day of Uhud, and he did not eat anything of his reward. We find nothing with which to shroud him, except for a namara. When we covered his head with it, his legs would come out, and when we covered his feet with it, he would come out. His head, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to cover his head with it, and to place pads on his feet, and among us is one for whom it has been gracious. “His fruit, he gifts it.” The wording is from Ishmael."
"2017","Abba Utbah bin Abdullah bin Utbah Al-Marwazi said: Yunus bin Nafi told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wash the person in ihram in the two garments in which he entered ihram, and wash him with water.” And Sidr, and shroud him in his two garments, and do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for on the Day of Resurrection he will be raised as forbidden,” Abu Abd said. Al-Rahman: Yunus bin Nafi’: nicknamed Abu Ghanim, Thiqah Marwazi, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated on his authority"
"2018","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, and Shababah, they said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ja’far, he heard Abu Nadra, On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best perfume is musk.”"
"2019","Anba Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Darhami told us: Umayyah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Mustamir bin Al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the best of your perfumes is musk.”"
"2020","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, in his hadith, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, that He told him that a poor woman had fallen ill, so he informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about her illness. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He would return to the poor and ask about them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If she dies, then notify me, and I will go out to her funeral at night.” They hated to wake the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so when the morning came the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of what had happened to her. He said: “Did I not command you to inform me of it?” They said: O Messenger of God! “We hated to wake you up at night.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and lined up people at her grave, and said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"2021","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahran, that Abba Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When a righteous man is placed on his bed, he says: Lead me, advance me.” The bad man was placed on his bed and said: “Woe to me, where are you taking me?”"
"2022","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, that he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the funeral is laid, and the men carry it on their necks, then if it is righteous, she said: Bring me, bring me, even if she is not righteous. She said: Oh, woe to her, where are you going with her? Everything hears her voice except man, even if he hears her. \a person who has been struck by shock\"""""""
"2023","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he conveyed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “Hurry up the funeral, for if it is righteous, then it is good that you will present it to him, and if it is not that, then evil that you will neglect.” \Your necks\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2024","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, who said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Umamah bin Sahl told me that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Hurry up the funeral. If it is good, bring it to goodness, and if it is not That was an evil that you put off your necks.”"
"2025","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Uyayna told us, he said: my father told me, he said: “I witnessed the funeral of Abdul-Rahman bin Samra Ziyad went out and walked in front of the bed, and he made men from Abdul Rahman’s family and his servants face the bed and walk on their heels. And they would say: Slowly, may God bless you. They kept moving, until when we were on the way to Marbad, Abu Bakra caught up with us on a mule. When he saw what they were doing, he attacked them with his mule, and whipped them with a whip. He said, “Be alone.” By the one who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. I saw that we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I were almost throwing sand with it, so the people dispersed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2026","Ali bin Hajar reported, on the authority of Ismail, and Hushaym, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, who said: You saw us with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we almost covered the funeral with sand.” This is the wording of the hadith of Hushaym."
"2027","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Amer bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, That he said: “If one of you sees a funeral and is not walking with it, let him stand until it leaves him or her until it is placed before you leave him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2028","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amer bin Rabi’ah Al-Adawi, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you see the funeral, stand up until it leaves you, or it takes place.”"
"2029","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Anba Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham, and Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see The funeral, then stand up, and whoever follows it, do not sit until it is placed.”"
"2030","Yahya bin Durst Al-Basri told me, he said: Abu Ismail told me, on the authority of Yahya, that Abu Salamah told him, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a funeral passes by you, stand up, and whoever follows it, do not sit until it is placed.” \"" 2031"""""
"2031","Yusuf ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, they both said: ""We never saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) attend a funeral and sit down until it was placed (on the ground)."""""
"2032","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abu Saeed said, and he told me Ibrahim bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq, he said: Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, He said: I heard Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a funeral procession, and he stood up, and Amr said in his hadith: “The The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a funeral passed by him, and he stood up.”"
"2033","Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told me, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Kharijah bin Zaid told me Ibn Thabit, on the authority of his uncle Yazid Ibn Thabit: “They were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a funeral took place, and the Messenger of God revolted.” God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and those with him revolted, and they did not stop standing until it was finished.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2034","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila. He said: Sahl bin Hunaif and Qais bin Saad bin Ubadah were in Al-Qadisiyah, so he passed by a funeral procession for them, and they got up, and it was said to them: From the people of the land, and they said: He passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at a funeral, so he stood up, and it was said to him: He is a Jew, so he said: “Isn’t he a soul?”"
"2035","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham, and Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: A funeral passed by, and the Messenger of God stood up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and we stood with him and said: O Messenger of God, it is only a Jewish funeral. He said: “Death is a terror, so if you see The funeral, so get up.” The wording is by Khaled."
"2036","Abba Muhammad bin Mansour said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We were with Ali, Then a funeral passed by, and they stood up for it, and Ali said: What is this? They said: The matter of Abu Musa, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only rose for a Jewish funeral, and then he did not return after that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2037","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad: that a funeral passed by Al-Hasan bin Ali and Ibn Abbas, so he stood up. Al-Hasan, and Ibn Abbas did not stand up, so Al-Hasan said: “Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stand up for the funeral of a Jew?” Ibn Abbas said: “Yes,” and then he sat down. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2038","Abba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abba Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He passed by a funeral for Al-Hasan bin Ali. And Ibn Abbas, so Al-Hasan stood up, but Ibn Abbas did not, so Al-Hasan said to Ibn Abbas: Didn’t the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stand up for her? Ibn Abbas said: “He stood up, then sat down.”"
"2039","Anba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Ibn Aliyah, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Ibn Abbas and Al-Hasan bin Ali passed They had a funeral, so one of them got up, and the other sat down, and the one who had risen said to him, “By God, I knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has risen.” The one who sat said: “I learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has sat.”"
"2040","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hasan bin Ali was sitting So he passed by a funeral procession, and the people stood until the funeral had passed, and Al-Hasan said: He only passed by the funeral of a Jew, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was there. “He did not like the funeral of a Jew to attend his head, so he got up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2041","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Al-Nadr, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that a funeral passed by the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he stood up. It was said that it was the funeral of a Jew. He said: “We only rose for the angels.”"
"2042","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj reported, saying: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: He stood up. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was attending a funeral that passed by him until he disappeared. He said: Abu al-Zubayr also told me that he heard Jabir saying: “He rose The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions attended the funeral of a Jew until it disappeared.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2043","Narrated by Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halah, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Qatada bin Rabi’i, It was said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a funeral procession, and he said: “He is at rest and at rest from him.” They said: And what is he at rest? And the one who is relieved from it? He said: “The believing servant will be relieved from the burdens and harms of this world, and the immoral servant will be relieved from it by the people, the land, the trees, and the animals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2044","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahim, he said: Zaid told me, and he is my father’s son. Unaysa, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Qatada, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when A funeral took place, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Relieved and freed from it; the believer dies, and is relieved from the burdens of this world.” And he set it up and harmed it, and the ungodly one will die, and the people, the land, the animals, and the trees will be relieved from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2045","Abba Ziyad bin Ayyub said: Ismail told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: He passed by a funeral, and it was praised well. Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is obligatory.” Another funeral passed by, and it was praised in a harsh manner. The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is obligatory,” so Omar said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He passed by a funeral, and it was praised well, so you said, “It is obligatory, it is obligatory,” and he passed by a funeral. Then she was praised for evil, and you said: It is due, it is due. He said: “Whoever you praise good, Paradise is certain for him, and whoever you praise is good, Paradise is certain for him. evil, and Hell will be necessary for it. You are God’s witnesses on earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2046","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar told us: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Ibrahim bin Amir, and his grandfather Umayyah bin Khalaf, who said: I heard Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: They passed by a funeral for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they praised him. It was good for her, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is obligatory.” Then they passed by another funeral, and they praised it badly, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “It is obligatory.” They said: O Messenger of God, your first and last saying: “It is obligatory”? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels are God’s witnesses in heaven, and you are God’s witnesses on earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2047","Anba Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik and Abdullah bin Yazid told us: Daoud bin Abi al-Furat told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, he said: I came to Medina and sat with Omar bin Al-Khattab, then a funeral passed and he was praised. It is good for its owner. Omar said: It is obligatory. Then he passed by another, and the owner of it was praised well. Omar said: It is obligatory, then he passed by a third. Then the owner was praised as evil, so Omar said: It is obligatory. He said: What is it obligatory, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I said as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any Muslim for whom four people testify that he is well, God will admit him to Paradise. We said: Or Three? He said: Or three? We said: Or two? He said: Or two"
"2048","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ahmad bin Ishaq told me, he said: Wahib told me, he said: Mansour bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was mentioned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he had perished in bad, and he said: “Do not mention your demise except with good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2049","Anba Humaid bin Masada, on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not curse the dead, for they have already accomplished what they put forward.”"
"2050","Abba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Three people follow the dead: his family, his money, and his work. Two of them will return: his family and his money, and one will remain, which is his work.”"
"2051","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “A believer has six characteristics over a believer: he visits him when he is sick, he witnesses him when he dies, he answers him when he calls him, and he greets him.” when he meets him, smells him when he sneezes, and advises him when he is absent or present.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2052","Abba Suleiman bin Mansour Al-Balkhi said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, he is Salam bin Sulaym, and Hannad bin Al-Sari reported on the hadith of Abu Al-Ahwas. On the authority of Ash'ath, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd, he said: Al-Baraa bin Azib said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do seven, and forbade us On the authority of seven: We were commanded to visit the sick, attend funerals, praise the sneezing person, honor the divider, support the oppressed, and disclose Peace, and responding to the supplicant, and forbade us from gold rings, and from silver vessels, and from cloaks, and cruel things, and from brocade, and silk. And the brocade"
"2053","Abba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Abther, who is Ibn al-Qasim Abu Zubaid, narrated to us on the authority of Burd, my brother Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Musayyab Ibn Rafi’, who said: I heard Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever follows a funeral in order to pray over it, will He will have one Qirat of reward, and whoever walks with the funeral procession until it is buried will have two Qirats of reward, and a Qirat is like Uhud.”"
"2054","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mughaffal, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever follows a funeral until it is finished, he gets two qirats, and if he returns before he finishes, he gets carat (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2055","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Wasil told us, he said: Sa`id bin Ubaid Allah told us, he is Al-Thaqafi, and his brother Al-Mughirah all, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The rider is behind The funeral, and he walks wherever he wants from it, and the child is prayed over.”"
"2056","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told me, he said: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his uncle Ziyad bin Jubayr bin Hayya, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one riding behind the funeral procession, and the one walking wherever he wants.” From it, and the child is prayed over.”"
"2057","Ishaq bin Ibrahim, Ali bin Hajar, and Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar walking in front of the funeral. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith is wrong, and they In it Ibn Uyaynah, Malik disagreed with him, he narrated it on the authority of Al-Zuhri with a mursal report. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2058","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid said: My father told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Mansour, Ziyad, and Bakr. All of them mentioned that they heard it from Al-Zuhri, so he narrated that Salim told him, that his father told him, that: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw He greeted Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman walking in front of the funeral procession. Bakr alone did not mention Uthman. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is also a mistake, and the correct thing is mursal, but this only came to me, and God knows best, because this hadith was narrated by Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of His father said that he was walking in front of the funeral, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and Omar were walking in front of the funeral, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was only according to what Al-Zuhri said. Ibn Al-Mubarak said: The custodians of Ibn Shihab were three: Malik and Muammar. And Ibn Uyaynah. If two people agree on a statement, we take it and leave the other’s opinion. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Blessed are these words according to the people of hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2059","Ali bin Hajar and Amr bin Zurarah reported, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran He is Ibn Husayn. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A brother of yours has died, so get up and pray for him.”"
"2060","Abba Muhammad bin Mansour said: Sufyan told us, he said: Talha bin Yahya told us, on the authority of his paternal aunt Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of her paternal aunt. Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, said: A boy from the Ansar was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pray over him. Aisha said: So I said: Blessed is this man. He is one of the birds of Paradise. He did not do evil, and it did not cause it to happen. He said: “Or something else? O Aisha, God’s creation.” Paradise, and created its people, and created them in the loins of their fathers. And He created Hell, and created its people, and created them in the loins of their fathers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2061","Anba Ismail bin Masoud told us: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed bin Ubaid Allah told us, he said: I heard Ziyad bin Jubayr talking, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one riding behind the funeral procession, and the one walking wherever he wants.” From it, and the child is prayed over.”"
"2062","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked He, peace and blessings be upon him, said about the children of the polytheists, and he said: “God knows best what they have been doing.”"
"2063","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Al-Aswad bin Aamir narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: “God knows best what they have been doing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2064","Anba Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: “God created them when He created them, knowing what they were doing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2065","Anba Mujahid bin Musa, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked Concerning the descendants of the polytheists, he said: “God knows best what they were doing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2066","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, who said: Abba Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, said: Ikrimah bin Khaled told me that Ibn Abi Ammar He told him, on the authority of Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, that a Bedouin man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he believed in him and followed him, then he said: I will emigrate. With you, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recommended him to some of his companions. When there was a campaign, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took captive sheep. So he swore, And he swore to him, so he gave his companions what he had sworn to him, and he was taking care of their backs. When he came, they gave it to him, and he said: What is this? They said: An oath given to you by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he took it and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What is this? He said: “I divided it for you.” He said: I did not follow you for this, but I followed you on the condition that I would be thrown here. He pointed to his throat with an arrow and die. Then he was entered into Paradise. He said: “If you believe in God, he will believe in you.” So they stayed for a little while. Then they rose up to fight the enemy, and he was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he was being carried. An arrow had struck him wherever he pointed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is it him?” They said: Yes. He said: “God has spoken the truth. So he believed him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, shrouded him in the robe of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then presented him and prayed over him. His prayers upon him: “Oh God, this is your servant. He went out as a migratory in your cause and was killed as a martyr. I am a witness against him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: What We know of someone who followed Ibn al-Mubarak on this, and the correct one is Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Shaddad ibn al-Hadi, and Ibn al-Mubarak is one of the imams. And perhaps someone else made the mistake, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2067","Abba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace One day, he went out and prayed the prayer for the family of someone as he prayed for the dead, then he went to the pulpit and said: “I am worthy of you, and I am a martyr.” \On you\"""""""
"2068","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, that Jabir bin Abd God told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to combine the two men who had been killed in one garment, then he would say: “Which one of them?” Should he recite more of the Qur’an? “So when one of them was pointed out to him, he would put it forward in the grave and say, ‘I will be a witness against these on the Day of Resurrection.’” He ordered that they be buried in their blood, and he did not pray over them, nor did they wash them. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This also we do not know of any of the trustworthy companions of Al-Zuhri followed Al-Layth on this narration, and disagreed with Al-Zuhri regarding it, and we have explained their disagreement over him in other places."
"2069","Anba Muhammad bin Yahya, and Nuh bin Habib, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Anba Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that a man who had converted to Islam came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he confessed to adultery, so he turned away from it, then He confessed, so he turned away from it, then he confessed, so he turned away from it, until he testified against himself four times, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Is your father mad? He said: No. He said: Are you safe? He said: Yes. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be stoned. When the stones fell on him, He fled, was caught, and was stoned until he died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said good to him, but did not pray for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2070","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I committed adultery and she was pregnant. So he gave it to its guardian, and he said: Be good to it, and when it delivers, bring it to me. When it delivered, he brought it. “So he ordered it, and she doubted.” She had her clothes on, then he stoned her, then prayed over her. “Then Omar said to him: Are you praying over her when she has committed adultery? ! He said: “She has repented with such a repentance that, if it were divided among seventy of the people of the city, it would be sufficient for them, and has she found anything better than that she repented?” By herself for God"
"2071","Anba Ali bin Hajar said: Anba Hushaym, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man freed six of his slaves. At the time of his death, he had no wealth other than them, so this reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he became angry about that and said: “I was thinking not to A prayer was performed over him, then he summoned his Mamluks and divided them into three parts, then he cast lots among them, freeing two and enslaving four.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2072","Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Amra, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani said: A man died in Khaybar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray for your friend, for he has committed wrong in the way of God.” So we searched his luggage and found that it contained Jewish beads worth two dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2073","Anba Mahmoud bin Ghailan told us: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought a man from the Ansar to pray over him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Bless your companion, for he owes a debt.” Abu Qatada said: It is mine, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ With loyalty? He said: With fulfillment, he said: Then he prayed over him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2074","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us: Yahya told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Salamah told us, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Peace be upon him with a funeral, and they said: O Prophet of God, bless her. He said: Did he leave behind any debt? They said: Yes. He said: Did he leave anything behind? They said: No. He said: Pray for your companion. A man from the Ansar, called Abu Qatada, said: Pray for him. May his debt be upon me. So he prayed for him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2075","Abba Nuh bin Habib, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Abba Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not pray for a man who was in debt. He brought a dead person and asked: “Is he in debt?” They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: “ “Bless your companion.” Abu Qatada said: They are upon me, O Messenger of God, so he prayed upon him. When God granted victory to His Messenger, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “I have more right over every believer than himself. Whoever leaves behind a debt is mine, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to his heirs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2076","Abba Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Abba Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus and Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would, when a believer died during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, owing a debt. He asks: “Has he left anything to pay off his debt?” If they say: Yes, he may pray upon him, and if they say: No, he says: “Pray upon your companion.” When God granted the victory On his Messenger, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Al-Futuh. He, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I have more right to the believers than they themselves. A debt, I must pay it off, and whoever leaves behind money, it belongs to his heirs.”"
"2077","Anba Ishaq bin Mansour told us: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr told us, he is the son of Muawiyah, he said: Samak told us, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, that a man killed himself with a mask, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for me, I will not pray for him.”"
"2078","Abba Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Dhakwan speaking, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever falls from a mountain and kills himself will be in the fire of Hell, wherein he will return and abide forever.” Therein forever, and whoever sips poison and kills himself, his poison will be in his hand and he will sip it in the fire of Hell to abide therein forever, and whoever kills himself With an iron, then something was cut off for me, meaning immortal. His iron was in his hand with which he would carry it into his stomach in the fire of Hell, immortal therein. \Never\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"2079","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Hujain bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: When Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul died The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was called for him to pray over him. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, 2104 rose and went to him, then I said: O Messenger of God! Shall you pray for Ibn Ubayy, when he said: On the day of such-and-such, such-and-such, and such-and-such, I will repeat it for him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and said: “Delay for me, O Omar.” When I told him more, he said: “I was given the choice, so I chose. If I had known that if I were to exceed seventy, he would be forgiven, I would have done more.” “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over him, then he left, and he only stayed for a short time until the two verses were revealed about Bara’ah: And do not pray for None of them ever dies, and do not stand on his grave. They disbelieved in God and His Messenger, and they died while they were sinners. I am still amazed at my audacity against the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on that day, and God and His Messenger know best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2080","Anba Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Ali bin Hajar said: Anba Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad reported, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Hamza, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for Suhail bin Bayda in the mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2081","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Hamza, that Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told him that Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray for Suhail bin Bayda except in the interior of the mosque.”"
"2082","Abba Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Abba Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Umamah bin Sahl told me: A woman complained about her poor family, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asking them about her, and he said: “If she died, then no Bury her so that I may pray over her.” Then she died, so they brought her to Medina after dark, and they found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He fell asleep, but they did not want to wake him up, so they prayed over her and buried her in Baqi al-Gharqad. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came in the morning, they came. So he asked them about her, and they said: She has been buried, O Messenger of God! We came to you and found you sleeping, and we did not like to wake you. So he said, “Go.” So he set off walking, and they went with him until they showed him her grave. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and they lined up behind him, so they prayed over her, and he said “Allahu Akbar” four times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2083","Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Kufi reported, on the authority of Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Your brother Al-Najashi has died, so get up and pray over him.” So he stood up and lined up with us as he would line up at a funeral, so he prayed over him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2084","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He mourned for the people the Negus on the day he died, then he went out with them to the prayer place, lined them up, and prayed over him. And he said “Allahu Akbar” four times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2085","Anba Muhammad bin Rafi’ said: It is Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned Al-Najashi to his companions in Medina, so they lined up behind him, so he prayed over him and said the takbir four times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2086","Abba Ali bin Hajar said: Abba Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A brother of yours has died, so get up and pray over him, and we formed two rows over him.”"
"2087","Anba Amr bin Ali said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: I heard Shu’bah say: The Hour will come, the Hour will come, Anba Abu Al-Zubair reported, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “I was in the second row on the day the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the Negus.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Zubayr: his name. Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Tadros, a Meccan, Shu’bah had a bad opinion of him, and Abu al-Zubayr was from al-Huffaz. Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated on his authority. Al-Ansari, Ayyub, and Malik bin Anas, so if he said: I heard Jabir, then it is correct, and he was deceiving, and he is more beloved to us about Jabir than Abu Sufyan, and this Abu Sufyan’s name is: Talha bin Nafi’, and by God, success. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2088","Anba Ismail bin Masoud said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your brother Al-Najashi has died, so get up and pray over him, so we got up. So We arranged for him as one would arrange for a dead person, and we prayed over him as one would pray over a dead person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2089","Abba Humayd bin Masada, on the authority of Abd al-Warith, said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Samurah, he said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon Umm Ka’b. She died in childbirth, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up to pray in the midst of her."
"2090","Abba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ammar, said: “I witnessed the funeral of a woman and a boy. The boy was brought forward from among the people next to him, and the woman was placed Behind him, he led the funeral prayer over them, and among the people were Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, Ibn Abbas, Abu Qatada, and Abu Hurairah, so I asked them about That, so they said: “the Sunnah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2091","Anba Muhammad bin Rafi’ said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Anba Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Nafi’, claiming that Ibn Umar: “He prayed for nine Funerals for all of them, so the men were made to face the imam, and the women were made to face the qiblah, so they lined them up in a single row, and the funeral of Umm Kulthum bint Ali was held. The wife of Omar ibn al-Khattab and a son of hers called Zaid, all together, and the imam at that time was Sa`id ibn al-Aas, and among the people was Ibn Abbas. And Abu Hurairah, and Abu Sa`id, and Abu Qatada, so the boy was placed next to the imam, “Then a man said: I denied that, so I looked at Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurairah, Abu Saeed, and Abu Qatada, so I said: What is this? They said: “It is the Sunnah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2092","Abba Ali bin Hajar, he said: Abba Ibn al-Mubarak, Al-Fadl bin Musa, and Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Hussein, who is the son of Dhakwan Al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the mother of so-and-so.” She died while giving birth, so he stood in the middle of her.” Ali said in his hadith: “A woman.”"
"2093","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned To the people, the Negus, and he went out with them, lined them up, and said “Allahu Akbar” to them four times."
"2094","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, who said: A woman from... The people of Al-Awali, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the best at treating the sick, and he said: “If she dies, notify me.” She died at night, and they buried her. They did not inform the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so when the morning came he asked about it, and they said: We hate to wake you up, O Messenger of God! So he came to her grave, prayed over her, and said “Allahu Akbar” four times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2095","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Amr bin Murrah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, that Zayd bin Arqam: “He prayed at a funeral, then said the takbir for it five times, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the takbir.”"
"2096","Narrated by Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abu Hamza bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying at a funeral, and he said: “ O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, pardon him, keep him well, honor his abode, widen his entrance, wash him with water, ice, and hail, and purify him. from sins just as a white garment is purified from filth, and replace it with a house better than its home, and a family better than its family, and a husband better than His wife, and protect him from the trial of the grave and the torment of the Fire.” Awf said: “I wished I were dead so that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would pray.” So dead"
"2097","Abba Harun bin Abdullah, he said: Ma’an narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Ubaid Al-Kala’i, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nafeer Al-Hadrami said: I heard Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying over a dead person, so I heard from His supplication, and he says: “O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, protect him, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, and wash him.” With water, ice, and hail, and purify it of sins as you purify a white garment of filth, and replace it with a better abode than its previous abode, and a good welcome. from his family, and a better husband than his wife, and admit him into Paradise, and save him from Hell.” Or he said: “Rescue him from the torment of the grave.”"
"2098","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, who said: Abba Abdullah, who said: Abba Shu’bah bin al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, who said: I heard Amr bin Maymun, narrating On the authority of Abdullah bin Rabi’ah Al-Sulami, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ubaid bin Khalid Al-Sulami, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He brought brotherhood between two men, and one of them was killed, and the other died after him. We prayed over him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What did you say? \They said: We prayed for him: O God"
"2099","Abba Ismail bin Masoud said: Abba Yazid, who is Ibn Zurai’, said: Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in prayer for the dead: “O God, forgive our living And our dead, and our witness, and our absent, and our male, and our female, and our young, and our old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2100","Abba Al-Haytham bin Ayyub, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Saad, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, he said I prayed behind Ibn Abbas at a funeral, and he recited the opening of the book and a surah, and he spoke aloud so that we could hear him. When he finished, I took him by the hand. So I asked him, and he said: “Sunnah and truth.”"
"2101","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar told us: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah, he said: “ I prayed with Ibn Abbas at a funeral, and I heard him reciting the Fatihah of the Book. When he left, I took him by the hand and asked him, saying: Are you reciting? He said: “Yes, it is the truth and the Sunnah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2102","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah, that he said: “The Sunnah in prayer over funerals is to The first takbeer is recited with the Umm al-Qur’an out of fear, then the takbeer is recited three times, and the salutation is made at the end.” Anba Qutaibah bin Sa’id said: He told us. Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suwayd al-Dimashqi, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Qais, and similar to that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2103","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Muti’, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, an infant. Aisha, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no dead body over which a group of Muslims can pray and reach the age of A hundred who would intercede unless they interceded on it.” Salam said: So I narrated it to Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, and he said: This is how Anas bin Malik narrated it to me, on the authority of the Prophet. May God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2104","Anba Amr bin Zurarah said: Anba Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, an infant of Aisha, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of the Muslims dies, and a group of people pray over him, and they reach the age of one hundred, and they will intercede, unless they will intercede on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2105","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Muhammad bin Sawa Abu Al-Khattab told us, he said: Abu Bakkar Al-Hakam bin Farukh told me, he said: He prayed with us. Abu Al-Malih was at a funeral, so we thought he had said the takbir, so he turned to us with his face and said: Straighten your ranks, and may your intercession improve. Abu Al-Malih: Abdullah bin Salit told me, on the authority of one of the mothers of the believers, Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me: “There is no dead person over whom a group of people prays, except that intercession is made for him.” So I asked Abu Al-Malih about the nation. He said: Forty (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2106","Anba Nuh bin Habib, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Anba Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays at a funeral will get a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is placed in the grave, will get two qirats, and the two qirats.” Like two great mountains.”"
"2107","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-Araj informed me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever attends a funeral until he prays over it, he will get a qirat, and whoever witnesses until it is buried, he will get two qirats.” It was said: What are two carats, O Messenger of God? He said: “Like two great mountains.”"
"2108","Anba Muhammad bin Bashar said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim man out of hope of seeking reward, prays over it, and buries it, gets two Qirats, and whoever prays over it, then If he returns before you are buried, he will return with a qirat of reward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2109","Abba Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us: Maslamah bin Alqama told us, he said: Abba Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, then leaves, will have a qirat of reward, and whoever follows it and prays upon her, then he sat until he had finished her fetus, for him two qirats of reward, each one of which is greater than the other.”"
"2110","Abba Suwayd bin Nasr said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hisham, and Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you see the funeral, stand up, and whoever follows it, do not sit until it is placed.”"
"2111","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he mentioned standing up for the funeral until it was laid, so Ali bin Abi Talib said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up.” Then he sat down.”"
"2112","Abba Ismail bin Masoud, he said: Abba Khaled, he said: Abba Shu’bah, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir informed me, on the authority of Masoud bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing up, so we stood up, and we saw him sitting down, so we sat down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2113","Anba Harun bin Ishaq said: Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “ We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at a funeral, and when we reached the grave, he did not turn away, so he sat down, and we sat around him as if he were \Our heads are birds\"""""""
"2114","Anba Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Coat them with their blood, for not a word is spoken about God but it will come on the Day of Resurrection bloody, its color the color of blood. And its scent is the scent of musk.”"
"2115","Abba Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: Abba Waki’, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of a man, called: Ubayd Allah bin Mu’iyah, he said: He was injured. Two Muslim men on the day of Taif. They were taken to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered that they be buried where they were wounded. “And Ibn Mu’iyah was born During the era of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2116","Anba Muhammad bin Mansour said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Qais told us, on the authority of Nabih Al-Anazi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: “He commanded those who were killed to be returned to their fields,” and they had been transported to Medina. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2117","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bury those killed in their battlefields.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Nabih al-Anazi was not narrated from him. Other than Al-Aswad bin Qais (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2118","Abba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Najiya bin Ka’b, on the authority of Ali, he said: I said: To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Your uncle, the misguided old man, has died. Who will protect him? He said: “Go and see your father, and do not speak of anything until you come to me.” So I saw him, then I came. “So he ordered me, so I took a bath,” and he called for me, and he mentioned I have a supplication that I have not memorized (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2119","Anba Amr bin Ali told us: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Makhrami told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, that he said: “They attacked someone else and attacked me as was done to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2120","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Amer told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, When Saad approached him, he said: “Make a sacrifice for me, and set up a monument against me, as was done to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2121","Abba Abdullah bin Muhammad Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrimi, on the authority of Hakam bin Salam al-Razi, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lahad is for us and the hardship is for others.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2122","I am Muhammad bin Bashar. He said: Ishaq bin Yusuf told us. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Hisham bin Amer. He said: We complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud, so we said: O Messenger of God! The digging upon us for every person is severe, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Dig and dig deep, and do well, and bury the two and three in One grave.” They said: “Who shall we advance, O Messenger of God?” He said: “The most of them presented the Qur’an.” He said: My father was the third of three in one grave. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2123","Anba Muhammad bin Muammar told us: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Humayd, who is Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham bin Amer, on the authority of his father, said: When it was the day of Uhud, some of the Muslims were injured, and people were wounded, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Dig and expand, and bury the two and three in the grave, and introduce the Qur’an to most of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2124","Anba Ismail bin Masoud reported, on the authority of Yazid, who is bin Zurai’, who said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, whose name is Nasr bin Imran Al-Basri, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “A red velvet was placed under the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was buried.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Abu Hamza: Imran bin Abi Ata is not strong, and Abu Hamza Nasr bin Imran Basri is trustworthy, and both of them narrate on the authority of Ibn Abbas."
"2125","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Musa bin Ali bin Rabah told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: I heard Uqba bin Amer. Al-Juhani said: “There were three hours during which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from praying or burying our dead: when “The sun rises early until it rises, and when the afternoon rises until the sun sets, and when the sun sets to set.”"
"2126","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir, saying “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech, and he mentioned a man from his companions who had died. He was buried at night and was shrouded in a useless shroud. The Messenger of God rebuked God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prohibits a person from being buried at night unless he is forced to do so.”"
"2127","Anba Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak said: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, he said: Humaid bin Hilal told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Amer said: When it was the day of Uhud, the people were struck by great distress, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Dig and expand, and bury.” The two and three are in a grave. They said: O Messenger of God! Who do we introduce? He said: “Introduce most of them to the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2128","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal. On the authority of Saad bin Hisham bin Amer, on the authority of his father, he said: “The wounds became severe on the day of Uhud, so this was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he greeted him and said: “Dig, dig wide, do good, and bury two and three in the grave, and recite the Qur’an to the most of them.”"
"2129","Abba Ibrahim bin Yaqoub said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dahama, on the authority of Hisham bin Amer, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Dig, expand, do good, and bury the two and the three. And they presented most of them with the Qur’an.”"
"2130","Abba Muhammad bin Mansour, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Hisham bin Amer, he said: He was killed On the day of Uhud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Dig, expand and do well, and bury the two and three in one grave. And they recited the Qur’an the most.” My father was the third of three, and he was the most recitative of the Qur’an. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2131","Al-Harith bin Miskin had a reading of it, and I hear, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Amr, Jabir, saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a servant “By God, Ibn Ubayy after he had been brought into his pit.” So he commanded him to be taken out, and he placed him on his knees, sprinkled some of his saliva on him, and clothed him. His shirt: “God knows best.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2132","Al-Hussein bin Harith narrated, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa narrated, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, he said: Amr bin Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir, He says: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Abdullah bin Ubayy to be taken out of his grave, and he placed his head on his knees and spit out.” In it was some of his saliva, and he clothed him with his shirt.” Jabir said: And God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2133","Anba Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari, on the authority of Saeed bin Amer, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, He said: “A man was buried in the grave with my father, and I did not feel comfortable until I took him out and buried him separately.”"
"2134","Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd, on the authority of his uncle Yazid bin Thabit said that they went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day, and he saw a fresh grave, and he said: “What is this?” They said: This is so-and-so, the servant of so-and-so, whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knew. She died at noon while you were fasting. So we did not like to We woke you up with it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and lined up the people behind him, “and he said the takbir over her four times,” then he said: “Let no dead person die among you.” As long as I remain before you except that which you have informed me of, for indeed my prayer is a mercy to him.”"
"2135","Anba Ismail bin Masoud said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He who passed with him told me The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on an outcropped grave. He led them in front of them and lined up behind him. “I said: Who is this, Abu Amr?” He said: Ibn Abbas"
"2136","Abba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim said: Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Tell me who saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As he said the salutation, he passed by an outcropped grave, prayed over it, and lined up his companions behind him. It was said: Who told you? He said: Ibn Abbas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2137","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Zaid bin Ali told us, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the grave of a woman after she was buried.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2138","Anba Ahmad bin Suleiman told us: Abu Nu’aym and Yahya bin Adam told us, they said: Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and prayed at the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah. When he returned, he was brought with a marred horse. So he rode him, and we walked with him.”"
"2139","Anba Harun bin Ishaq said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, and Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, requested that something be built over the grave, or that something be added to it, or that it be plastered.” Suleiman bin Musa added: “Or that something be written on it.”"
"2140","Anba Yusuf bin Saeed said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the graves being blocked, or building on them, or anyone sitting on them.”"
"2141","Abba Imran bin Musa, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about plastering graves.”"
"2142","Anba Suleiman bin Dawud said: Anba Ibn Wahb told me: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Thumama bin Shafi told him, he said: “We were with Fadalah bin Ubaid in the land of Byzantium. A friend of ours died, so Fadalah ordered his grave to be leveled. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, orders that it be settled.”"
"2143","Anba Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abu Al-Hayaj, he said: He said: Ali: Shall I not send you to do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to do: “Do not leave a high grave unless you have leveled it, and no image in a house unless you have leveled it.” \You erased it.\"""""""
"2144","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, and I have forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals for more than three days.” For a few days, abstain from whatever you like, and I forbade you from wine except from something to drink from, so drink from all of the vessels, and do not drink any intoxicating drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2145","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Subay’, he said: Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father: “He was in a gathering in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I had forbidden you to eat meat.” Sacrifices except three, so eat, feed, and store what you wish, and I have mentioned to you not to be shunned in certain circumstances: the scavengers, the zafaat, and the neqir. And you, be careful of what you see, and avoid every intoxicant, and I forbid you from visiting graves, so whoever wants to visit a grave So let him visit him, and do not say, 'Forsaking him.'\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
